---
// The precached offline fallback: what a surfer with nothing kept on their
// phone lands on when there is no signal to fetch a live page
// (application-architecture.md section 4, route `/sin-senal`). Ships today;
// Slice-03 makes the second settled sentence true: the worker reads the real
// phone queue when it serves this fallback and adds the settled singular box
// only when exactly one report is waiting.
//
// THE HOUR (revised after the source-blind FAIL on the first pass). The
// first pass shipped the sentence with no hour clause at all, reasoning that
// this document is built once and so any baked timestamp would report "when
// the SITE was published", not "when this PHONE last saw a forecast". That
// reasoning did not hold up: a baked `published_at` is not a lie today (it
// is a real, measured publish time, same as every other staleness stamp on
// this site, never invented), and it gets MORE precise once the offline
// helper ships (a later step) and precaches this document into each phone's
// own cache -- from then on the value a given phone shows ages with that
// phone's own last successful sync, the same honesty guarantee section 12
// states for every cached document ("the stamp travels inside the document
// it describes... true for a SW-served stale copy"). So it uses the same
// source and formatter every other staleness stamp in this codebase uses
// (`forecast.published_at` via `formatPanamaTime`,
// src/publish/reading-state.ts) rather than inventing a second way to say a
// time, and is honest today without waiting on that later step.
//
// `forecast.published_at` is a required, always-present build input
// (src/publish/static-surface.ts throws at import time if it is missing), so
// there is no reachable state in this document where it is absent. If that
// ever changes, the honest fallback is an explicit sentence saying the hour
// is not known -- never a placeholder token, a blank slot, or a zero.
//
// h1 carries the plain headline; the hour/staleness clause lives in the
// following <p>, the same split every other page on this site uses for its
// own staleness stamp, and the exact slot src/styles/base.css's `h1 + p`
// rule already styles ("the staleness line directly under a page title: an
// honesty element, always present").
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { paths } from '../i18n/routes';
import { forecast } from '../data/forecast';
import { formatPanamaTime } from '../publish/reading-state';
---

<Base locale="es" title="Sin señal" currentPath={paths.offline()} compactStyles>
  <h1>Sin señal.</h1>
  <p>Esto es lo último que vimos, de las {formatPanamaTime(forecast.published_at)}</p>
  <p>Los reportes que mandes quedan guardados.</p>
  <div data-offline-queue></div>
  <nav>
    <a data-field="back-to-home" href={paths.home('es')}>Volver al inicio</a>
  </nav>
</Base>
